--------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROVENANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This work is original. No code, schema definition, table name, column name,
or data model in this project was copied, ported, paraphrased, or otherwise
derived from any existing ERP product — commercial or open source.

Two published, non-proprietary conceptual sources informed the VOCABULARY of
the domain model and are acknowledged here. Neither contributed code:

  * ISA-95 / IEC 62264 — the equipment-hierarchy vocabulary
    (enterprise / site / area / work centre / work unit). Used as naming
    for the location hierarchy; the structure is this project's own.

  * REA (W. E. McCarthy, "The REA Accounting Model", The Accounting Review,
    1982) — the resource / event / agent duality concept, which informs the
    paired-flow design of the ledger. An academic accounting model, not a
    product.

Identifier and code formats follow GS1, UN/CEFACT, ISO 8601 and ISO 4217
where interoperability calls for it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The core has a single runtime dependency:

  * psycopg (LGPL-3.0-or-later) — PostgreSQL adapter.
    https://www.psycopg.org/

The list is kept deliberately short and is enforced by an allowlist in
tests/test_layer_boundary.py: adding a dependency to the core is a
deliberate act, because this distribution inherits its licence and its
supply chain.
